WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.540
{Chapter 01}

00:13.200 --> 00:15.499
It has to be the high-end ones.

00:15.500 --> 00:16.660
Don't be stupid.

00:17.120 --> 00:20.039
Sweet bean jelly that cost 500 yen each?

00:20.040 --> 00:22.920
Your mother would be rolling
in her grave if she knew that.

00:26.840 --> 00:29.300
Oh, Takumi, are you going out?

00:29.970 --> 00:31.640
Just to the field.

00:34.100 --> 00:37.140
Takumi, there's something
I've been meaning to ask you.

00:37.850 --> 00:39.730
That incident with the baseball team...

00:40.100 --> 00:42.310
You weren't involved, were you?

00:44.860 --> 00:47.819
Not that I'm really expecting
you to actually answer me.

00:47.820 --> 00:50.569
Why would you ask me that at this point?

00:50.570 --> 00:52.489
Because you seem depressed.

00:52.490 --> 00:54.199
They suspended our team.

00:54.200 --> 00:55.360
Of course I'd feel depressed.

00:56.700 --> 00:58.079
You're right.

00:58.080 --> 01:02.040
If you have baseball taken away from you,
you have nothing left.

01:02.750 --> 01:06.380
But you've lost weight, haven't you?

01:07.550 --> 01:09.050
Is something troubling you?

01:10.630 --> 01:11.840
Don't touch me!

01:13.010 --> 01:14.639
Don't touch my shoulder.

01:14.640 --> 01:16.180
Takumi!

01:16.970 --> 01:19.929
Fine! I won't mention it again.

01:19.930 --> 01:21.310
Do whatever you want.

01:21.600 --> 01:24.229
Oh, you were so close, Makiko.

01:24.230 --> 01:25.570
Close with what?

01:26.360 --> 01:29.319
It's because you touched
a pitcher's shoulder.

01:29.320 --> 01:31.609
You need to be more careful.

01:31.610 --> 01:34.450
I touched my <i>son's</i> shoulder.

01:52.090 --> 01:57.680
I've heard it said so many times

01:58.390 --> 02:04.560
How it's not going to work out

02:05.520 --> 02:11.070
That nothing will change

02:11.360 --> 02:17.580
Even if I pretended not to listen

02:18.030 --> 02:21.369
I knew it all

02:21.370 --> 02:24.539
I learned this from you

02:24.540 --> 02:32.540
That it's not a failure, even when it is

02:33.930 --> 02:40.519
When I thrust my feelings
on to the drifting clouds

02:40.520 --> 02:47.439
The quiet melodies push me forward

02:47.440 --> 02:53.949
Because the sky is so vast and free

02:53.950 --> 03:01.580
I decided that I wouldn't cry anymore

03:06.960 --> 03:09.959
All right, let's get to it before it rains.

03:09.960 --> 03:12.550
Rain? Look how clear the skies are.

03:14.550 --> 03:16.379
Is that coming this way?

03:16.380 --> 03:17.679
Yeah.

03:17.680 --> 03:19.550
You notice how humid it's gotten?

03:20.850 --> 03:22.600
Let's warm up that shoulder.

03:34.530 --> 03:35.530
What is it?

03:36.400 --> 03:37.400
Behind you.

03:40.070 --> 03:41.370
Otomurai.

03:43.290 --> 03:44.910
Coach...

03:45.750 --> 03:47.210
Let me borrow that for a second.

03:47.750 --> 03:48.750
Yes, sir.

03:49.210 --> 03:51.210
Harada, I'll catch for you.

03:51.500 --> 03:52.500
Pitch to me.

03:54.050 --> 03:55.720
What? Am I not up to your standards?

03:56.050 --> 03:57.800
No, it's just...

04:00.550 --> 04:03.470
Can you really catch my pitches, Coach?

04:08.690 --> 04:10.940
You've got some nerve.

04:12.020 --> 04:13.269
Go for it, Takumi.

04:13.270 --> 04:15.990
I get to watch you
from a different position.

04:16.650 --> 04:17.820
Different position?

04:37.760 --> 04:40.339
Is that Harada's best pitch?

04:40.340 --> 04:42.139
No, he can do more.

04:42.140 --> 04:43.259
I figured as much.

04:43.260 --> 04:46.930
He's not holding back for my sake, is he?

04:47.560 --> 04:50.729
The next pitch will be his.

04:50.730 --> 04:53.899
Was he testing me?

04:53.900 --> 04:55.110
Honestly.

04:55.780 --> 04:58.070
Give me one right down the middle, Harada!

04:58.490 --> 05:01.110
Show me the fastest pitch you got!

05:18.880 --> 05:19.880
Was that it?

05:19.880 --> 05:20.880
Yes.

05:22.970 --> 05:25.180
Give me three more in that same spot.

05:38.570 --> 05:41.319
Can't you give it back to
me a little more carefully?!

05:41.320 --> 05:45.660
I was ready to laugh and say how
unimpressed I was with his pitching.

05:47.030 --> 05:49.080
Come here, Harada, and make it quick.

05:52.750 --> 05:55.170
You want to play, don't you, Harada?

05:57.960 --> 06:03.050
With our activities suspended, there hasn't been much
hope for a game, let alone even time to practice.

06:03.340 --> 06:06.299
I hope you've realized
how powerless you are.

06:06.300 --> 06:07.140
Coach!

06:07.141 --> 06:09.060
Quiet! Let me talk here!

06:10.180 --> 06:11.559
Listen up, Harada.

06:11.560 --> 06:14.229
You're still in junior high.

06:14.230 --> 06:17.320
You don't get to play in
a game if it's canceled.

06:17.820 --> 06:20.190
That's where you're at. Got it?

06:21.780 --> 06:24.070
Please stop, Coach!

06:27.700 --> 06:30.080
Then what about you, Coach?

06:30.830 --> 06:33.960
What makes you so great that
you can sit there and judge us?

06:34.750 --> 06:38.000
They took baseball away from you too!

06:40.250 --> 06:42.209
You need to cut this shit out, Harada!

06:42.210 --> 06:44.299
Think about who you're speaking to!

06:44.300 --> 06:47.139
Didn't you want to play baseball?

06:47.140 --> 06:50.719
Didn't you want to compete as a coach?

06:50.720 --> 06:55.230
You said that I was going to start
the first game of the tournament!

06:55.730 --> 06:57.360
Yes, I did!

06:59.690 --> 07:02.190
I pitch and Gou catches.

07:02.860 --> 07:08.320
Are you telling me that you never wanted to see
what it'd be like to coach a game like that?

07:13.870 --> 07:17.880
You're such an insufferable brat.

07:22.380 --> 07:25.879
I'll be getting our activities
resumed before long.

07:25.880 --> 07:27.510
Make sure you stay in shape.

07:28.470 --> 07:30.349
I won't let you do what you want next time.

07:30.350 --> 07:31.760
What did you say?

07:33.060 --> 07:36.020
I'm not letting any of you
tell me what to do again.

07:39.560 --> 07:42.980
There's still a lot you don't know.

07:43.940 --> 07:48.320
Including just how fun a sport baseball is.

07:49.320 --> 07:50.779
Why don't you give it a serious shot?

07:50.780 --> 07:56.000
Try playing not for yourself
but for your team instead.

07:57.080 --> 07:58.870
Harada, Nagakura.

08:00.540 --> 08:03.050
We're going to make it
to nationals next year.

08:05.050 --> 08:06.050
Coach.

08:07.220 --> 08:09.970
I'll take you to nationals with me.

08:10.930 --> 08:12.300
What was that?

08:12.810 --> 08:15.310
I'm willing to make you a
coach that wins nationals.

08:17.230 --> 08:19.309
Well, now that you've made that bold claim,

08:19.310 --> 08:22.440
I'm going to make sure you do what
needs to be done to keep that promise.

08:32.530 --> 08:34.830
I have a favor to ask, sir.

08:35.490 --> 08:39.329
I heard that you were close with
Yokote Second Junior High's principal.

08:39.330 --> 08:40.709
Yes, I suppose.

08:40.710 --> 08:43.590
Could you ask them for a game?

08:43.880 --> 08:45.340
With Yokote's baseball team?

08:48.470 --> 08:50.930
Yokote Second Junior
High's baseball team...

08:51.760 --> 08:56.849
Didn't they win the district
tournament final 8-1 or something?

08:56.850 --> 08:58.480
It was 9-1.

08:59.190 --> 09:00.939
I doubt it, then.

09:00.940 --> 09:02.859
I see.

09:02.860 --> 09:06.899
If I were Yokote's
principal, I would decline.

09:06.900 --> 09:08.360
We're just not the same caliber.

09:09.700 --> 09:11.069
Please!

09:11.070 --> 09:13.620
I can step in and help
with the negotiation!

09:14.240 --> 09:17.870
Mr. Tomura, please try not to rush things.

09:18.160 --> 09:24.630
The only thing you need to worry about doing is
leading the baseball team in a wholesome manner.

09:26.800 --> 09:28.130
I apologize.

09:29.470 --> 09:32.429
Please refrain from
taking action on your own.

09:32.430 --> 09:34.760
The baseball team does not belong to you.

09:35.140 --> 09:37.970
It belongs to Nitta East Junior High.

09:53.030 --> 09:55.410
Takumi! It's Kaionji!

09:56.490 --> 09:57.490
Hello?

09:58.290 --> 10:01.869
<i>The coach wants to talk to
us after the opening ceremony.</i>

10:01.870 --> 10:03.420
<i>We're meeting by the nets.</i>

10:03.960 --> 10:07.419
Does that mean we can start
practicing again tomorrow, Captain?

10:07.420 --> 10:09.920
Today's the last day
of summer vacation!

10:07.750 --> 10:09.209
<i>I think so.</i>

10:09.210 --> 10:11.760
<i>We might be able to make
the rookie game in the fall.</i>

10:12.760 --> 10:19.060
<i>If I'm being honest,
I'm a little jealous of you underclassmen.</i>

10:19.970 --> 10:21.019
<i>Harada.</i>

10:21.020 --> 10:22.020
Yes?

10:23.020 --> 10:26.770
<i>It goes without saying that I'll be contacting
Nobunishi and everyone else too. Okay?</i>

10:27.610 --> 10:30.940
Captain, I hate Nobunishi and his friends.

10:32.440 --> 10:36.449
But I can live with it as long
as it means I can play baseball.

10:36.450 --> 10:39.489
<i>I don't care what you want.</i>

10:39.490 --> 10:42.749
<i>All I care about is that
we have a functional team.</i>

10:42.750 --> 10:43.710
Right.

10:43.710 --> 10:44.710
<i>Bye, then.</i>

10:48.710 --> 10:49.710
Pardon me!

10:50.800 --> 10:51.960
Is Takumi here?!

10:52.590 --> 10:55.219
This is my house. Where else would I be?

10:55.220 --> 10:57.090
Oh, you've got a point.

10:58.050 --> 11:00.259
Did you get a call from Kaionji?

11:00.260 --> 11:01.469
Just now, yeah.

11:01.470 --> 11:04.600
Isn't it awesome?!
We get to play baseball again tomorrow!

11:05.690 --> 11:06.480
Gou!

11:06.481 --> 11:08.190
Oh, Seiha!

11:09.020 --> 11:10.899
You're looking more manly.

11:10.900 --> 11:13.109
Have you put on weight?

11:13.110 --> 11:14.030
Do you mean that?

11:14.031 --> 11:16.529
I've been eating three square meals a day.

11:16.530 --> 11:18.239
I eat all my vegetables too!

11:18.240 --> 11:21.949
Oh, Seiha, you act so spoiled around Gou.

11:21.950 --> 11:26.000
I guess you look for attention
because Takumi never gives you any.

11:35.720 --> 11:37.260
I'm sorry.

11:39.930 --> 11:42.809
I've caused a lot of
trouble for all of you.

11:42.810 --> 11:47.899
But after I was able to get the principal's
and other teachers' understanding,

11:47.900 --> 11:50.810
they allowed us to
resume our team activities.

11:51.820 --> 11:52.820
Harada.

11:53.650 --> 11:55.400
Are you listening?

11:55.740 --> 11:56.740
No, sir.

11:59.370 --> 12:05.290
Coach, all the seniors will
be retiring soon, won't we?

12:05.870 --> 12:07.670
Hold on, Kaionji.

12:08.370 --> 12:11.499
Yes, seniors would normally
retire around this time.

12:11.500 --> 12:15.380
But this year, I'd like you
to stay on a little longer.

12:15.760 --> 12:17.129
What do you mean?

12:17.130 --> 12:20.930
I want to set up a exhibition
game and treat it like a formal one.

12:21.470 --> 12:24.059
We didn't get to participate
in the district tournament.

12:24.060 --> 12:28.140
I can't send you off
with so much left undone.

12:29.730 --> 12:31.859
You're letting us play?

12:31.860 --> 12:33.320
That's my intention.

12:33.650 --> 12:35.320
Who will we get to play?

12:35.780 --> 12:38.320
I want to play Yokote Second Junior High.

12:38.820 --> 12:39.820
Yokote?

12:41.660 --> 12:43.369
Please let us play them, Coach!

12:43.370 --> 12:47.039
I don't care if it's not a real
game if we can play Yokote!

12:47.040 --> 12:48.040
Right?

12:49.250 --> 12:52.330
However, I haven't gotten
the school to sign off on this.

12:52.750 --> 12:54.710
They told me we're
just on different levels.

12:58.380 --> 12:59.839
I see.

12:59.840 --> 13:01.840
I'm sorry to interrupt,

13:02.260 --> 13:03.549
but I'm going home.

13:03.550 --> 13:05.720
I can't be late for my cram school.

13:06.720 --> 13:10.939
And also, here is my letter of resignation.

13:10.940 --> 13:12.230
Nobunishi.

13:14.190 --> 13:16.399
Are you really going to quit?

13:16.400 --> 13:17.480
Yes, sir.

13:17.900 --> 13:18.900
I...

13:19.610 --> 13:21.490
I just hate him.

13:23.370 --> 13:24.870
That's my only reason.

13:27.540 --> 13:29.000
Hold on a second.

13:29.410 --> 13:31.210
What kind of reason is that?

13:31.830 --> 13:35.000
Are you really going to run
from a little freshman kid?

13:36.960 --> 13:42.050
I never really liked
teamwork in the first place.

13:44.010 --> 13:46.640
But I did have fun some of the time.

13:47.430 --> 13:52.640
I knew I was getting better, but I
was putting up with it the whole time.

13:53.020 --> 13:55.019
That's what baseball is, isn't it?

13:55.020 --> 14:00.150
You're the one who taught us that putting
the team first is what's most important.

14:01.150 --> 14:02.280
I did.

14:02.650 --> 14:04.869
Then what about Harada?

14:04.870 --> 14:10.039
Do you really think he's
playing baseball for the team?

14:10.040 --> 14:11.960
Wait, Nobunishi...

14:17.800 --> 14:22.089
Tell me, Harada, have you
ever wanted to win a tournament?

14:22.090 --> 14:26.300
Or wanted the team to improve?

14:26.680 --> 14:27.810
No.

14:28.470 --> 14:31.980
But I also know that I can't
play baseball by myself.

14:32.940 --> 14:37.310
I guess my only goal is to
throw the best pitch I can.

14:40.320 --> 14:42.570
You're going to fail, Harada!

14:43.200 --> 14:48.829
You can't achieve your dreams
by doing whatever you want to!

14:48.830 --> 14:49.830
I won't accept it!

14:52.290 --> 14:53.580
Excuse me.

14:54.290 --> 14:55.580
Nobunishi!

14:56.250 --> 14:59.590
After all these years, you're
really just going to end it like this?

15:01.000 --> 15:02.049
Sorry.

15:02.050 --> 15:05.969
You're the only one I feel
bad about doing this to.

15:05.970 --> 15:07.300
I'm really sorry.

15:14.730 --> 15:16.019
Nobunishi.

15:16.020 --> 15:18.359
Just let him go, Coach!

15:18.360 --> 15:20.229
What do you mean?

15:20.230 --> 15:22.990
I knew this whole time.

15:24.740 --> 15:28.240
I knew how much strain
he was putting on himself.

15:29.370 --> 15:32.240
But I told him to hold it in for the team.

15:33.660 --> 15:37.040
So please just let him
do what he wants now.

15:41.380 --> 15:43.380
Coach! What if...

15:46.130 --> 15:48.799
What if Yokote asks us for a game?

15:48.800 --> 15:50.140
What did you say?

15:51.140 --> 15:52.640
- Baseball Team
- Baseball Team

15:52.643 --> 15:54.890
Do you have an idea?

15:55.350 --> 15:58.729
Don't tell me your plan
is to just go and beg them.

15:58.730 --> 16:00.609
No, I'm not going to beg.

16:00.610 --> 16:04.319
I'm just going to meet with their
captain and talk to him directly.

16:04.320 --> 16:06.150
You mean Kadowaki?

16:06.490 --> 16:08.530
Who else would it be?

16:08.950 --> 16:11.780
But he's a real slugger.

16:12.490 --> 16:16.290
Rumors say that big high schools
are trying to scout him even now.

16:16.830 --> 16:19.669
You know Kadowaki?

16:19.670 --> 16:22.789
I just talked to him at the
district tournament last year.

16:22.790 --> 16:25.300
Will he really agree to play us?

16:26.340 --> 16:30.760
I'm going to try to tempt him so
that he'll be begging to face us.

16:31.430 --> 16:33.560
It might just work.

16:34.010 --> 16:35.010
How?

16:35.310 --> 16:36.389
Harada.

16:36.390 --> 16:37.429
Yes?

16:37.430 --> 16:40.940
You need to pitch to
Kadowaki and strike him out.

16:41.650 --> 16:46.440
If you can do that, knowing his
personality, he's going to want his revenge.

16:47.240 --> 16:51.030
He's not one to sit idly by after
getting struck out by a freshman.

16:51.870 --> 16:53.950
After that, I'll just need to talk to him.

16:55.990 --> 16:58.369
That's crazy, Kaionji.

16:58.370 --> 17:01.079
This is a big responsibility, Harada.

17:01.080 --> 17:02.080
Yes.

17:02.081 --> 17:04.000
Look, I don't think you understand.

17:04.800 --> 17:08.340
They say Kadowaki's a talent that
only comes around once every ten years.

17:09.470 --> 17:11.840
I know he'll be able to take down Kadowaki.

17:15.930 --> 17:17.469
Hey, Takumi.

17:17.470 --> 17:19.230
It's someone from the baseball team.

17:20.480 --> 17:21.480
Hello?

17:22.020 --> 17:27.229
<i>Harada, we're meeting Kadowaki
at Yokote's central park in two days.</i>

17:27.230 --> 17:28.230
Okay.

17:28.740 --> 17:31.360
<i>Coach is going to
give us a ride in his car.</i>

17:31.700 --> 17:34.619
<i>It'll be me, you, and Nagakura going.</i>

17:34.620 --> 17:35.699
<i>Got it?</i>

17:35.700 --> 17:37.869
Understood. I'll see you then.

17:37.870 --> 17:39.199
<i>Hold on!</i>

17:39.200 --> 17:40.869
<i>Don't you have any questions for me?</i>

17:40.870 --> 17:42.369
About what?

17:42.370 --> 17:45.629
<i>Like how I was about to
get Kadowaki to agree to this.</i>

17:45.630 --> 17:47.550
<i>What do you think I told him?</i>

17:48.300 --> 17:49.340
I don't know.

17:50.720 --> 17:53.090
<i>Man, you really are cold.</i>

17:53.890 --> 17:59.309
<i>I asked him if he wanted to
face a real 140 km/h pitch.</i>

17:59.310 --> 18:01.439
<i>That got him to bite.</i>

18:01.440 --> 18:05.400
<i>But I wasn't joking.</i>

18:23.210 --> 18:24.210
Sorry to keep you.

18:24.790 --> 18:25.790
Yo.

18:28.460 --> 18:29.550
Is that him?

18:29.960 --> 18:31.049
Yes.

18:31.050 --> 18:32.669
He's so skinny.

18:32.670 --> 18:35.719
Can he really pitch that well?

18:35.720 --> 18:37.600
Yes, but only fastballs.

18:38.510 --> 18:41.430
We've got tests every day at our school.

18:42.020 --> 18:44.940
All the seniors are in exam mode.

18:45.350 --> 18:48.859
Yeah, but you're getting
in with a sports scholarship.

18:48.860 --> 18:50.569
You don't have to worry about exams.

18:50.570 --> 18:53.989
Yeah, but everyone around
me is studying like crazy.

18:53.990 --> 18:56.569
I was bored out of my mind.

18:56.570 --> 18:59.580
But then I got a call from you.

18:59.990 --> 19:03.539
It sounded interesting, so here we are now.

19:03.540 --> 19:06.209
Oh, so you were just bored.

19:06.210 --> 19:09.210
I mean, I didn't quite
believe everything you said.

19:09.670 --> 19:10.670
But...

19:11.960 --> 19:13.840
he looks like the real deal.

19:31.940 --> 19:32.940
Strike.

19:34.240 --> 19:36.700
I see. You weren't lying.

19:41.740 --> 19:42.740
Ball.

19:46.040 --> 19:47.710
Hey, catcher.

19:48.460 --> 19:51.839
Is that pitcher following your signals?

19:51.840 --> 19:53.169
Yes.

19:53.170 --> 19:58.339
In that case, since this isn't a real game, how
about we leave all the cheap tricks out of it?

19:58.340 --> 20:01.350
Can you have him throw
the fastest pitch he's got?

20:01.970 --> 20:02.970
Okay.

20:24.910 --> 20:26.039
Strike.

20:26.040 --> 20:27.250
Time out!

20:30.250 --> 20:32.339
That was freaking blazing.

20:32.340 --> 20:35.420
Kadowaki's timing was completely off.

20:37.090 --> 20:39.180
Your fingers are shaking.

20:40.510 --> 20:42.260
I guess I'm pretty excited.

20:43.430 --> 20:45.180
Could you throw that again?

20:47.100 --> 20:48.100
What is it?

20:49.560 --> 20:51.560
It's nothing. I got it.

21:04.200 --> 21:05.619
Home run.

21:05.620 --> 21:07.750
Will it make it to the stands?

21:08.120 --> 21:09.580
Just barely.

21:15.590 --> 21:17.260
Takumi!

21:21.800 --> 21:24.180
Summer's peak came and went

21:26.560 --> 21:32.849
That's what the weather report said

21:32.850 --> 21:39.360
But it still feels like
the city is restless

21:47.200 --> 21:55.200
The evening bells of 5 p.m.
resonate inside my heart today

22:02.130 --> 22:08.535
Clouding me with something
convenient like "destiny"

22:20.511 --> 22:24.199
It's the final fireworks of the year

22:24.200 --> 22:27.910
I will remember them for years to come

22:27.911 --> 22:31.619
I will remember them for years to come

22:31.620 --> 22:33.475
